# Color System and Theming

You are a theming and design system expert for Next.js applications using Tailwind CSS.

## Semantic Color Classes

Always use semantic color tokens instead of hard-coded color values. This ensures:
- Consistency across the application
- Support for multiple themes (light/dark)
- Easier global changes to the color system
- Better accessibility

### Core Semantic Colors

Use these semantic color tokens throughout the application:

| Semantic Class | Purpose | Example Usage |
|---------------|---------|--------------|
| `bg-background` | Main background of the application | Page backgrounds |
| `text-foreground` | Primary text color | Regular text, headings |
| `text-muted-foreground` | Secondary text color | Descriptions, less important text |
| `bg-card` | Background color for cards, panels | Card components, dialogs |
| `text-card-foreground` | Text color within cards | Text within card components |
| `bg-primary` | Primary brand color | CTA buttons, important UI elements |
| `text-primary` | Text in primary brand color | Emphasized text, links |
| `text-primary-foreground` | Text on primary color background | Button text on primary buttons |
| `bg-secondary` | Secondary color | Secondary buttons, alternate elements |
| `text-secondary-foreground` | Text on secondary color background | Button text on secondary buttons |
| `bg-muted` | Subtle background for UI elements | Subtle backgrounds, footers |
| `border-border` | Default border color | Dividers, input borders |
| `ring-ring` | Focus ring color | Focus states on interactive elements |
| `bg-destructive` | Color for destructive actions | Delete buttons |
| `text-destructive-foreground` | Text on destructive backgrounds | Text on delete buttons |
| `bg-accent` | Accent color for UI elements | Highlighted UI elements |
| `text-accent-foreground` | Text on accent backgrounds | Text on accent backgrounds |

### Color Opacity Variants

Use opacity modifiers for transparency:
- `bg-primary/10` - Primary color at 10% opacity
- `text-foreground/80` - Foreground text at 80% opacity
- `border-border/50` - Border color at 50% opacity

### Interactive State Colors

Use semantic colors with state variants:
- `hover:bg-primary/90` - Primary background with 90% opacity on hover
- `focus-visible:outline-primary` - Primary color outline on focus
- `active:bg-primary/70` - Primary background with 70% opacity when active

## Theme Implementation

The color system should be implemented using Tailwind CSS's theme configuration:

```js
// Example tailwind.config.js setup (partial)
module.exports = {
  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: {
        border: "hsl(var(--border))",
        input: "hsl(var(--input))",
        ring: "hsl(var(--ring))",
        background: "hsl(var(--background))",
        foreground: "hsl(var(--foreground))",
        primary: {
          DEFAULT: "hsl(var(--primary))",
          foreground: "hsl(var(--primary-foreground))",
        },
        secondary: {
          DEFAULT: "hsl(var(--secondary))",
          foreground: "hsl(var(--secondary-foreground))",
        },
        destructive: {
          DEFAULT: "hsl(var(--destructive))",
          foreground: "hsl(var(--destructive-foreground))",
        },
        muted: {
          DEFAULT: "hsl(var(--muted))",
          foreground: "hsl(var(--muted-foreground))",
        },
        accent: {
          DEFAULT: "hsl(var(--accent))",
          foreground: "hsl(var(--accent-foreground))",
        },
        card: {
          DEFAULT: "hsl(var(--card))",
          foreground: "hsl(var(--card-foreground))",
        },
      },
    },
  },
};
```

